From: X-Wrt developers
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: free incomplete RX frames before page pool teardown

A scattered packet can remain in q->skb across NAPI polls. Its pages have
already left the descriptor ring, so descriptor cleanup alone cannot
release them. Free the partial skb after NAPI quiescence and clear its
saved descriptor metadata before destroying the page pool.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2776,6 +2776,14 @@
 	struct airoha_eth *eth = qdma->eth;
 	int qid = q - &qdma->q_rx[0];
 
+	/* NAPI is quiesced by the caller. A partial scattered frame owns
+	 * pages that are no longer present in the RX descriptor ring.
+	 */
+	dev_kfree_skb_any(q->skb);
+	q->skb = NULL;
+	q->rx_msg0 = 0;
+	q->rx_msg1 = 0;
+
 	while (q->queued) {
 		struct airoha_queue_entry *e = &q->entry[q->tail];
 		struct airoha_qdma_desc *desc = &q->desc[q->tail];
